2220	 *    On 1.18 that directive is a hard config error, so HTTP/2 is folded into the
2221	 *    `listen` line instead.
2222	 *  - A TLS server block is emitted ONLY when the certificate files were verified
2223	 *    to exist on this machine. A config that references a missing certificate
2224	 *    stops nginx from starting at all — the worst possible outcome.
2225	 *
2226	 * Every interpolated value is pre-validated: domains by DOMAIN_RE, paths by
2227	 * PATH_RE, ports as integers. The file is written over SFTP, so no shell is
2228	 * involved in producing it.
2229	 */
